# p01 nothing asserted (the open-world default)
#
# LinkML option: none. This is what a record looks like when option0 is not enforced, and what
# every other option degrades to if the reason is dropped.
#
# Present: the assay, its specimen input, and a measurement datum as its output.
# Absent: any value specification, numeric value, unit, or statement about why.
# (The even emptier case, no assay and no datum at all, is base.ttl on its own.)
#
# A consumer can infer nothing about the value: under the open-world assumption the missing
# triples may exist elsewhere. They cannot tell "not applicable", "not collected", "withheld",
# or "lost in transit" apart, and they cannot tell this record from p12 (asked, answer unknown).

@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://example.org/encounter/> .
@prefix BFO:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_> .
@prefix IAO:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_> .
@prefix OBI:  <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_> .

ex:glucoseAssay1 a owl:NamedIndividual , OBI:2100072 ;
    BFO:0000050 ex:encounter1 ;
    OBI:0000293 ex:specimen1 ;
    OBI:0000299 ex:glucoseDatum1 .

ex:glucoseDatum1 a owl:NamedIndividual , IAO:0000109 ;
    IAO:0000136 ex:specimen1 .
    # no OBI:0001938 has value specification triple
    # no datum status or reason about this datum
